# Unauth Direction

Always treat `docs/product/MVP_STEERING.md` as the product source of truth.

Also reference when needed:
- `docs/product/PRODUCT_PRINCIPLES.md`
- `docs/product/TERMINOLOGY.md`
- `CLAUDE.md` (product direction + engineering rules)

Unauth is a post-purchase loss accountability platform.

The MVP is Shopify/Gorgias payout control + evidence checklist + merchant rules + attribution/recoverability + manual recovery cases + recovery board + partner rulebook v1.

Do not frame Unauth primarily as a fraud/risk network.

Do not use accusatory language like fraudster, bad actor, blacklist, guilty, caught, scammer, or cross-merchant accusation.

Use operational language:
- payout exposure
- support payout case
- evidence strength
- merchant rule fired
- recommended action
- loss attribution
- recoverability
- recovery owner
- prevention opportunity
- policy leakage
- partner accountability

Merchant rules make recommendations. Unauth surfaces evidence and next actions.

The Gorgias widget must stay compressed. It should be a 4-line decision card, not a full dashboard.

Full investigation belongs in the Unauth case page.

Recovery operation belongs in the recovery board.

Partner recoverability rules belong in the partner rulebook.

Do not overbuild automatic carrier claims, AI contract extraction, network benchmarks, WMS/ERP integrations, or full enterprise APIs until the MVP workflow is proven.
